<title>UK: Storehouse firm after trading statement.</title>
<headline>Storehouse firm after trading statement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Storehouse Plc were 18p higher at 275-1/2p by 0830 GMT after the retailer said group sales on a like-for-like basis rose nine percent in the six weeks to December 24.</p>
<p>Total group sales in the period were up by 18 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;After some recent disappointing Christmas sales statements from other high street chains, the market has certainly welcomed the Storehouse results,&quot; one senior dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;The shares have underperformed over the past few months so a bit of a bounce is to be expected.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
